Netflix Global Content Insights Dashboard

This project presents an interactive Power BI dashboard analyzing the global content catalog of Netflix to uncover trends in content growth, audience targeting, and geographic distribution.
The goal of this project is to demonstrate how business intelligence tools can transform raw entertainment data into actionable insights about platform strategy and viewer focus.

The dataset used in this analysis was sourced from Kaggle and cleaned using Power Query before being modeled and visualized in Microsoft Power BI.

Project Objectives :

-Analyze how Netflix’s content library has evolved over time
-Identify differences in growth between movies and TV shows
-Explore how content is distributed globally
-Examine rating patterns to understand audience targeting
-Identify dominant genres shaping the platform’s catalog

Tools & Technologies Used :

-Power BI (dashboard design and visualization)
-Power Query (data cleaning and transformation)
-DAX (KPI creation and calculated measures)

Key Insights :

-Netflix experienced rapid catalog expansion after 2015, indicating aggressive global growth and investment in content production.
-Movies make up the largest share of titles, but TV shows show consistent long-term growth, reflecting Netflix’s increasing focus on binge-worthy serialized content.
-Mature audience ratings such as TV-MA and TV-14 dominate the platform, suggesting a strong focus on adult and young-adult demographics.
-Drama, documentaries, and international content are among the most common genres, highlighting Netflix’s emphasis on storytelling diversity and global reach.
-Content production is heavily concentrated in North America, Europe, and Asia, showing where Netflix’s strongest production ecosystems exist.

What This Project Demonstrates :

-This dashboard showcases practical data analyst skills including:
-Cleaning and restructuring messy categorical data
-Creating meaningful KPIs using DAX
-Designing intuitive and interactive dashboards
-Building visual hierarchy for storytelling
-Translating data into business-focused insights

